{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And now, etc.</b> If it is true that I have found favor in Your eyes — <b>make Your ways known to me, I pray.</b> What reward do You give to those who find favor in Your eyes?" "<b>And I will know You, so that I may find favor in Your eyes.</b> And I will know through this measure of Your recompense — what is this 'finding favor' that I have found in Your eyes. And the resolution of <b>so that I may find favor</b> — so that I may recognize how great is the reward of finding favor." "<b>And see that this nation is Your people.</b> That You not say 'I will make you into a great nation and these I will leave' — see that they are Your people from aforetime; and if You reject them, I do not rely on those who will issue from my loins to endure; and the recompense of my reward You must make known to me in this people. And our Sages interpreted it in tractate Berakhot (7a) — but I have come to settle the verses according to their contextual sense and according to their order."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:21.838636534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}